[139.367152, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Struts Exfil campaign\r\n====================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: struts-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.167\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1190\r\nExploit Public-Facing Application\r\n[initial-access] step 1: Struts2\r\nOGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164)\r\nT1505.003 Web Shell\r\n[persistence] step 2: JSP webshell\r\nplanted\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 3: shell execution\r\nT1560.001 Archive via Utility\r\n[collection] step 4: stage archive\r\nfor exfil\r\nT1048\r\nExfiltration Over Alternative Protocol [exfiltration] step 5: exfiltrate\r\nover HTTPS\r\nT1098.004 SSH Authorized Keys\r\n[persistence] step 6:\r\nauthorized_keys backdoor\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 7: cron persistence\r\nT1070.002 Clear Linux or Mac System Logs\r\n[defense-evasion] step 8: selective\r\n"]
[139.367337, "o", "auth-log wipe\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\nCVE-2023-50164 CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 CWE=CWE-552\r\nAn attacker can manipulate file upload params to enable paths traversal and under some\r\ncircumstances this can lead to uploading a malicious file which can be used to perform Remote\r\nCode Execution.Users are recommended to upgrade to version\r\nref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/176157/Struts-S2-066-File-Upload-Remote-Code-Ex\r\necution.html\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.167\r\nc2 update-struts[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]struts[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n"]
[139.367507, "o", "\f"]
