[199.479468, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Intrusion Analysis Report — Struts Exfil Campaign\n\n## Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor conducted a multi-stage post-compromise intrusion against server `struts-prod-01` (`10.10.246.1`) `/disk/etc/hosts:2`. The initial compromise leveraged Apache Struts2 OGNL Remote Code Execution (`CVE-2023-50164`) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17` to deploy a JSP web shell, followed by database archiving, exfiltration over HTTPS, persistence placement via cron and SSH `authorized_keys`, and selective wiping of system authentication logs. While security alerts in `/sas/alerts.json:2` caught partial activity (web shell, staged archive, cron job), silent persistence mechanisms and exfiltration endpoints were revealed through forensic disk examination.\n\n---\n\n## Attack Chain Analysis & Evidence Mapping\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access & Exploitation (T1190)\n- **Description:** The threat actor probed and exploited an OGNL injection vulnerability (`CVE-2023-50164`) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17` present in the installed `struts2-core.jar` library `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`, `/sas/alerts.json:28`.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - `GET /struts2-showcase/ HTTP/1.1` probe recorded in `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:393`.\n  - Alert trigger for vulnerable library recorded at `/sas/alerts.json:28` and `/sas/baseline.json:3`.\n\n### Step 2: Persistence via Web Shell (T1505.003)\n- **Description:** Exploitation permitted path traversal and file upload capabilities, resulting in a JSP web shell dropped into the web application directory.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - JSP web shell file created at `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\n  - Web shell alert entry in `/sas/alerts.json:2`.\n  - Upload attempt recorded in `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`.\n\n### Step 3: Shell Execution & Command Execution (T1059.004)\n- **Description:** Web shell interaction and root SSH session allowed command execution across system context.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - SSH root session established from `198.51.100.167` `/disk/var/log/secure:213`.\n  - Command execution via cron re-drop script `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`.\n\n### Step 4: Collection & Data Staging (T1560.001)\n- **Description:** Sensitive database contents were dumped and compressed into a hidden tarball archive staged in `/tmp/.cache/`.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - Database archive file present at `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`.\n  - SAS alert for exfil archive at `/sas/alerts.json:11`.\n\n### Step 5: Data Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol (T1048) — *Silent Action*\n- **Description:** Staged data was exfiltrated out of the environment via HTTP POST requests to the external C2 address.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - Logged HTTP GET/POST exfiltration request recorded in `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`.\n  - *Note:* Omitted from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### Step 6: SSH Authorized Keys Persistence (T1098.004) — *Silent Action*\n- **Description:** Attacker planted an unauthorized SSH key into root's `authorized_keys` file for persistent administrative access.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - Public key entry in `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`.\n  - *Note:* Omitted from `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### Step 7: Scheduled Task / Cron Persistence (T1053.003)\n- **Description:** A cron job was added under the `tomcat` user spool to periodically fetch and execute external payload scripts.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - Cron spool entry at `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`.\n  - Alert entry in `/sas/alerts.json:19`.\n\n### Step 8: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (T1070.002) — *Silent Action*\n- **Description:** Attacker selectively deleted authentication records and log files to cover intrusion traces.\n- **Evidence:**\n  - Anti-forensic wiping artifact recovered at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\n  - Gap in authentication entries in `/disk/var/log/secure:213`.\n\n---\n\n## Identified Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n| Entity Type | Indicator | Source Citation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Attacker Origin IP | `198.51.100.167` | `/disk/var/log/secure:213`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:27` |\n| C2 Domain | `update-struts.example.cn"]
[199.47965, "i", "` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:28` |\n| Cryptomining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.struts.evil:3333` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:29` |\n| Cryptomining Wallet | `4A000000000000000000e40b218944d0` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:30` |\n| Malicious Web Shell | `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` | `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1` |\n| Staged Exfiltration File | `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1` |\n| Cron Persistence File | `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5` |\n| SSH Backdoor File | `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |\n\n---\n\n## Business & Security Impact\n- **Confidentiality Loss:** Database dump exfiltrated over HTTPS `/disk/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log:116`, `/disk/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz:1`.\n- **Integrity Loss:** System configuration compromised with unauthorized SSH keys `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` and cron jobs `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`; system logs wiped `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\n- **Availability Risk:** Remote code execution capabilities allow full host takeover `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\nEOF\n"]
