[215.429768, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[215.429798, "o", "> "]
[215.429887, "o", "## Remediation & Patching Guidance\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[215.430176, "o", "1. **Upgrade Struts2 Component:** Upgrade `struts2-core` library to patched versions (e.g., Apache Struts 2.5.33, 6.3.0.2, or later secure releases) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[215.430432, "o", "2. **Web Shell Neutralization:** Quarantine and remove `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[215.430717, "o", "3. **Application Directory Restrictions:** Configure write permissions on `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` so Tomcat process cannot write executable scripts into static directories.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[215.43147, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@ec2bee70e55c:/app# "]
[229.349969, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis report details system, application, and security configuration deficiencies identified on host `struts-prod-01` (`10.10.246.1`) `/disk/etc/hosts:2`. In addition to running outdated vulnerable library components (`struts2-core.jar`) `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`, several system-level configuration weaknesses enabled persistent access, unauthorized code execution, and evasion of auditing.\n\n---\n\n## Identified Baseline & Configuration Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Outdated Vulnerable Application Component (BAS-01 / CHK-05)\n- **Deficiency:** Deployment of vulnerable Apache Struts2 library file `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`.\n- **Evidence:** `/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:28`.\n- **Impact:** Allows unauthenticated remote code execution and arbitrary file creation (`CVE-2023-50164`) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`.\n\n### 2. Excessive Web Server Directory Write Permissions\n- **Deficiency:** Web application static directory `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` had write permissions enabled for the web service user.\n- **Evidence:** File created at `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\n- **Impact:** Allowed the attacker to drop executable JSP web shells into public web routes.\n\n### 3. SSH Key Authorization Security & Auditing Gaps\n- **Deficiency:** Lack of periodic auditing or integrity checking on administrative `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`.\n- **Evidence:** Unauthorized SSH key added at `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` without detection or alerting in SAS feeds `/sas/alerts.json:2`.\n- **Impact:** Silent persistence established with persistent root administrative access.\n\n### 4. Unmonitored User Cron Spool Execution\n- **Deficiency:** Insufficient monitoring and controls over `/var/spool/cron/` user crontabs.\n- **Evidence:** Cron entry in `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5` fetching external scripts via curl `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`.\n- **Impact:** Automated persistence and payload re-infection.\n\n### 5. Authentication Logging & Local Log Integrity Deficiencies\n- **Deficiency:** Local system logs (`/var/log/secure`) lacked remote central logging and append-only immutability.\n- **Evidence:** Selective log deletion artifact recovered at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` and missing log window in `/disk/var/log/secure:213`.\n- **Impact:** Attacker successfully erased authentication traces without alerting endpoint security monitors.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations for Configuration Hardening\n1. Implement centralized, read-only remote log shipping (e.g., via rsyslog/fluentd) to prevent local log tampering `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\n2. Restrict Tomcat execution permissions and enforce read-only filesystems for static assets (`/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/`) `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\n3. Implement automated file integrity monitoring (FIM) for SSH authorized keys (`/root/.ssh/authorized_keys`) `/disk/root/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` and cron directories (`/var/spool/cron/`) `/disk/var/spool/cron/tomcat:5`.\nEOF\n"]
